when there are multiple environments like DEV Prod and test 
and when a pipline is triggered it should run on respective environments

We need to have multiple tools to be install to fullfill our CI/CD needs for that we need huge amount of memory t2.micro or medium won't work for high workloads



RBAC 

if not using RBAC in jenkins we can use AWS SSO or Azure AD

to acheive in jenkins we need a plugin called "Role-based Authorization Strategy"
Once installed to activate it we need to tweak some settings 
under manage Jenkins>Security>Authorization
We will have a option "Role Based Stratergy"

Once That is done we will be enabled with a option "Manage and Assign Roles" under Security in Manage Jenkins Page 

Security>Manage and Assign Roles>
We can add Roles like admin with full access and developer with only read access and devops engineer with full access

And we need to define on which items they can have this access for that we need to add "item roles"

So we're done with roles and item roles now we need add Users

Once we're done with creating users we need to assign these roles to the users
under manage Jenkins>Manage and Assign Roles>Assign Roles
And also assign Item roles java and python which we created to respetcive users

